Package: lex1d
Type: Package
Title: Fast Least-Squares Partition of One-Dimensional Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Sriram", "Natarajan", email = "nsram@users.noreply.github.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Partitions one-dimensional data into k contiguous clusters with a low
    within-cluster sum of squares (one-dimensional k-means, optimal scalar
    quantization). The default method seeds local refinement with an exact dynamic
    program over a coarse summary of at most 4096 groups; an exact dynamic program
    (Fisher 1958) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1958.10501479> is also provided. Optional
    non-negative weights. The interface and result follow 'Ckmeans.1d.dp' for a
    fixed k, including its tie rule. The C++ core is shared with the Python and
    Scala implementations in the same repository.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/nsram/lex1d
BugReports: https://github.com/nsram/lex1d/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), Ckmeans.1d.dp
Config/testthat/edition: 3
